# No end-of-line conversion, on any platform, for any file.
#
# stamp.py cache-busts by hashing the raw bytes of data.js, fx.js and the
# stylesheet. Git for Windows defaults to core.autocrlf=true, which would give
# the working copy CRLF while the repo and GitHub Pages keep LF - so the stamp
# written into the pages would be the hash of a file nobody is ever served, and
# readers would sit on a stale cached copy with no way to tell.
#
# Everything here is generated LF and served LF. Nothing should touch that.
* -text
